# Git and reviews

- Never `git push` to `main`. Create a focused branch, open a PR, merge after CI and CodeRabbit.
- One concern per PR. Do not stack a second change on the same branch.
- Commit as `area: concrete change`. `Closes #N` in the body only when the user named a real issue.
- After opening a PR: wait for CI (`Test`) and CodeRabbit. Fix what they flag. Repeat until CI is green and CodeRabbit has no new blocking comments.
- Run `npm run test:all` before you say the work is done.
- Read `AGENTS.md` (short). If `COMMIT.md` exists locally, follow it for commit wording.
